+| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
+| `display_name` | Public user profile name displayed to colleagues | UTF-8 String (1 to 120 characters) | User's full name | Sanitized against invisible Unicode characters and control codes |
+| `timezone` | Canonical IANA timezone used for date formatting | 15 canonical timezones (e.g. `America/New_York`, `UTC`) | `UTC` | Localizes ticket creation, audit timestamps, and SLA due date displays |
+| `avatar` | User profile photograph or custom avatar | PNG, JPEG, or WebP image file (<= 2 MiB) | Default letter icon | Re-encoded server-side via Pillow; SVG uploads rejected fail-closed |
+| `current_password` | Verification of existing credentials before password update | String matching current password | Required on change | Prevents unauthorized password changes on unattended sessions |
+| `new_password` | Updated local authentication password | Min 12 chars (Min 14 for Server Admins) | User-supplied | Salted and hashed via Argon2id with server-side pepper |
+| `passkeys` | FIDO2 / WebAuthn biometric security keys | Platform (Touch ID/Hello) or Cross-Platform (YubiKey) | None enrolled | Hardware-bound cryptographic public key authentication |
+| `totp_enabled` | Time-based one-time password (RFC 6238) 2FA | 6-digit verification code from authenticator app | Disabled | Requires AAL2 step-up challenge to disable once activated |
+| `recovery_codes` | Single-use emergency account recovery backup codes | 10 alphanumeric single-use codes | Generated on 2FA setup | Stored hashed in PostgreSQL; invalidated upon individual consumption |
+| `linked_identities` | External OIDC, Google, GitHub, or LDAP accounts | Verified external provider identity claims | Primary login card | Enables single-sign-on without password storage; unlinking requires AAL2 |
+
+### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs (Personal Settings)
+
+- **display_name:** The user's public identity rendered across comments, avatar badges, activity feeds, and assignment menus. Cleaned server-side using Unicode guards to strip zero-width spaces and spoofing homoglyphs.
+- **timezone:** The user's localized timezone selection, chosen from 15 canonical IANA timezones (such as `America/New_York`, `Europe/London`, `Asia/Tokyo`, `UTC`). All timestamps remain stored canonically as UTC in PostgreSQL and are formatted to the user's local offset on the client.
+- **avatar:** Profile picture uploaded via `PUT /api/v1/auth/me/avatar`. The backend enforces a strict 2 MiB size cap and validates the raster payload via content-sniffing. Dangerous vector formats (SVG) are rejected fail-closed to eliminate XSS risks, and images are re-encoded to sanitized PNG format.
+- **current_password:** Required whenever a user modifies their local password via `POST /api/v1/auth/me/password`. Guards against session hijacking by requiring proof of current knowledge before modifying credentials.
+- **new_password:** The updated password. The platform enforces strict entropy requirements: standard users must supply at least 12 characters, while users possessing the `SERVER_ADMIN` role must supply at least 14 characters.
+- **passkeys:** WebAuthn credentials registered via `POST /api/v1/auth/webauthn/register:start` and `:finish`. Passkeys support both platform biometrics (Touch ID, Face ID, Windows Hello) and cross-platform hardware tokens (YubiKey). Each enrolled key displays nickname, enrolled date, and a non-intrusive **Test Passkey** verification button.
+- **totp_enabled:** Activates Time-Based One-Time Password verification for authenticator applications (Aegis, Google Authenticator, 1Password). Enrolled via QR code and verified with a 6-digit challenge code. Disabling TOTP requires mandatory AAL2 step-up verification.
+- **recovery_codes:** A set of 10 single-use emergency recovery codes generated when two-factor authentication is configured. Each code can be used exactly once to regain account access if hardware tokens or authenticator apps are lost.
+- **linked_identities:** Manages connected third-party enterprise identity cards (Google Workspace, GitHub, GitLab, Okta, Active Directory LDAP). Users can link multiple external accounts to a single local identity or unlink secondary providers after completing AAL2 step-up verification.
